    "seoDescription": "A guide to Kalooki etiquette \u2014 respect, sportsmanship, pace, and conduct at the table.",
    "body": [
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "_key": "b0",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "_key": "s0",
            "text": "July 16, 2024",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "_key": "b1",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "_key": "s1",
            "text": "Kalooki has been a staple in social circles for decades. Beyond the cards, the game carries a rich tradition of etiquette. Here\u2019s the guide that ensures everyone has a great time at the table.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "_key": "b2",
        "style": "h2",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "_key": "s2",
            "text": "1. Respect the Host",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "_key": "b3",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "_key": "s3",
            "text": "Arrive on time, bring a small gift if appropriate, and offer to help set up or tidy up. A gracious guest sets a positive tone for the entire session.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "_key": "b4",
        "style": "h2",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "_key": "s4",
            "text": "2. Know the Rules",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "_key": "b5",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "_key": "s5",
            "text": "Familiarise yourself with the rules before sitting down. Some groups use house rules \u2014 clarifying beforehand avoids confusion. Review the official Super Kalooki rules here .",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "_key": "b6",
        "style": "h2",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "_key": "s6",
            "text": "3. Mind Your Manners",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "_key": "b7",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "_key": "s7",
            "text": "Keep conversation pleasant. Kalooki is a social experience as much as a competitive one. A respectful atmosphere makes the game enjoyable for everyone.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "_key": "b8",
        "style": "h2",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "_key": "s8",
            "text": "4. Be a Good Sport",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "_key": "b9",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "_key": "s9",
            "text": "Celebrate victories with humility and accept losses gracefully. Compliment good plays. Good sportsmanship enhances the camaraderie that makes Kalooki special.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "_key": "b10",
        "style": "h2",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "_key": "s10",
            "text": "5. Stay Focused",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "_key": "b11",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "_key": "s11",
            "text": "Avoid prolonged distractions \u2014 phones, unnecessary breaks, side conversations that slow the game. Staying engaged shows respect for everyone\u2019s time.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "_key": "b12",
        "style": "h2",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "_key": "s12",
            "text": "6. Play at a Reasonable Pace",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "_key": "b13",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "_key": "s13",
            "text": "Neither too slow nor too fast. A balanced rhythm keeps the game moving while giving everyone time to think through their turn.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "_key": "b14",
        "style": "h2",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "_key": "s14",
            "text": "7. Express Gratitude",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "_key": "b15",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "_key": "s15",
            "text": "At the end, thank the host and fellow players. A simple gesture of appreciation builds lasting friendships around the table.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "_key": "b16",
        "style": "h2",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "_key": "s16",
            "text": "Conclusion",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "_key": "b17",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "_key": "s17",
            "text": "Kalooki is more than a card game \u2014 it\u2019s a social ritual. By following these guidelines, every game is played in the spirit of fairness, respect, and genuine enjoyment.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "_type": "article",
    "title": "Kalooki Game",
    "slug": {
      "_type": "slug",
      "current": "kalooki-game"
    },
    "excerpt": "Learn about the Kalooki card game \u2014 Jamaican origins, how rounds work, scoring, and why it's loved worldwide.",
    "publishedAt": "2024-07-05T12:00:00.000Z",
    "seoTitle": "Kalooki Game",
    "seoDescription": "Learn about the Kalooki card game \u2014 Jamaican origins, how rounds work, scoring, and why it's loved worldwide.",
    "body": [
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "_key": "b0",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "_key": "s0",
            "text": "July 5, 2024",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "_key": "b1",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "_key": "s1",
            "text": "Kalooki is a card game played with four to six players using multiple decks of 52 cards and jokers. A form of Contract Rummy, it originated in Jamaica and is now enjoyed by players worldwide. The game rewards strategic thinking while keeping an element of luck that makes every session fresh.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "_key": "b2",
        "style": "h2",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "_key": "s2",
            "text": "The Objective",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "_key": "b3",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "_key": "s3",
            "text": "The goal is to be the first player to get rid of all the cards in your hand by forming sets (three or more cards of the same rank) and runs (four or more consecutive cards of the same suit) across nine rounds, each with a specific contract requirement.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "_key": "b4",
        "style": "h2",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "_key": "s4",
            "text": "How a Round Works",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "_key": "b5",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "_key": "s5",
            "text": "Each player is dealt a number of cards based on the round. The remaining cards form a draw pile; the top card starts the discard pile. On each turn, draw a card, optionally lay down your contract, and discard one card. The first player to clear their hand wins that round.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "_key": "b6",
        "style": "h2",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "_key": "s6",
            "text": "Scoring",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "_key": "b7",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "_key": "s7",
            "text": "After nine rounds the player with the lowest total score wins. Numbered cards are worth face value; face cards are 10 points; red aces are 1 point; black aces are 15 points; and jokers carry a heavy 50-point penalty if caught in your hand.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "_key": "b8",
        "style": "h2",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "_key": "s8",
            "text": "Why Kalooki?",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "_type": "block",
        "_key": "b9",
        "style": "normal",
        "markDefs": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "_type": "span",
            "_key": "s9",
            "text": "Kalooki works equally well as a casual social game or in a competitive setting \u2014 which is why Super Kalooki brings it online for all skill levels, from solo AI practice to live multiplayer with friends.",
            "marks": []
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
]